This sequence avoids two costly mistakes: building new Governance on top of unresolved ownership, and using Geography for authoritative jurisdiction decisions before its isolation and integrity are established.

The first vertical slice should remain narrow: “current members may post.” Use the existing Admit/End facts rather than pretending Suspend is implemented. Evaluate the policy against authoritative Membership facts, enforce the agreed concurrency protocol, and persist the decision evidence atomically with the post. Keep production routes disabled until all release gates are satisfied.

