## 7. How far are we from the goal?

My assessment is that we have a substantial research and design foundation, but we are still in the transition from architecture to verified integration.

- The Membership kernel has strong reported test evidence within its implemented scope.
- Governance and Geography are not yet safe, authoritative replacements for their legacy counterparts.
- Authorization and concurrency protocols have promising bounded-model evidence, but not end-to-end application verification.
- The first cross-domain vertical slice and production cutovers remain outstanding.
- The latest reported evidence score is 6/30; it should not be presented as a percentage of total implementation completed.

The next meaningful milestone is not another broad architecture document. It is security containment completed, the blocking decisions recorded, and one protected cross-domain command proven against the real application infrastructure.

That milestone will show whether the architecture works in practice—and will give us a reliable foundation for the subsequent Governance, Geography and Forum implementation.
